+## 2026-10-24 bounded peer repair: review-a38a551c738ff9bc
+
+Baseline generator SHA-256
+`3dad3d6e93d0411f112e69c0ae2961885200e6c9970a76f879627ebc8e16a6a2`
+had no task-local tests and relied on independent random draws despite claiming
+that every four-demo lesson varied arithmetic and placement. A protected-Racket
+probe over 24 natural lessons / 120 labels found three harmful windows: the
+`signed_2_minus_8` rival survived twice and `fixed_height_1` survived once.
+Because color 8 was always left of color 2, the shortcut “place two columns
+right of color 2” also matched all 120 generated labels, even though it matched
+only two of four canonical pairs.
+
+The selected version 3.0.0 repair adds a deterministic four-slot curriculum.
+Every four consecutive natural examples now include both signs of the height
+difference, both bar orders, at least two absolute differences, and at least two
+output columns. Explicit `col_8`/`col_2` overrides may place either color on the
+right, while the rightmost-bar-plus-two bound remains enforced. The canonical
+Racket rule was not changed.
+
+Final source binding:
